 ## Falsifiable package rule
 
-When a claim package states or describes a vulnerability report made through GitHub private vulnerability reporting, check it against S073 in this order. (1) The package must record, for the target repository, how enablement was established: the repository's own SECURITY.md or contributing text naming the route, or a dated record of the repository's public page showing the “Report a vulnerability” (`S073.txt:569`) control (the enablement condition itself is at `S073.txt:564`); the page gives no other method, and a bare assertion that the feature is enabled does not satisfy this step. (2) If no such record exists, the package must instead cite the repository's security-policy route or the issue fallback quoted at `S073.txt:566`, and must not describe the report as a private-reporting submission. (3) A package that names the feature with neither a step (1) record nor a step (2) citation fails this rule. A package that states a fix was merged from the reporter's private fork fails unless it also records the maintainer's merge, because only the maintainer can merge (`S073.txt:578`).
